T device or a service"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account by certificate rather than by secret. # What is and is not copied Only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"public_cert_pem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the certificate. The "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"private key stays where its custodian put"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Why a restart rustls builds its "},{"code":"RootCertStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" once, when the listener is constructed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change took effect. Defaults to "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cacertificate\/mtlstrustanchor","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mtlsTrustAnchor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"mtlsTrustAncho